description: System architecture and domain boundaries
alwaysApply: true
Architecture
Applications

The platform contains:

apps/api — NestJS backend
apps/web — Next.js customer storefront
apps/admin — Next.js administration
apps/reseller — Next.js reseller portal
apps/mobile — Ionic mobile application
Shared packages

Use shared packages for:

types
validation
API client
configuration
UI components where appropriate
Backend

NestJS is the central business platform.

Business domains should remain separated:

auth
users
customers
catalog
inventory
carts
orders
shipping
payments
accounting
resellers
promotions
CMS
notifications
reports

Avoid giant services containing unrelated business logic.

Clients

Clients are responsible for:

presentation
navigation
interaction
local UI state
API communication

Clients are NOT authoritative for:

prices
stock
payments
accounting
commissions
permissions
order status
Infrastructure

Initial infrastructure:

AWS EC2
Docker
Nginx
AWS RDS PostgreSQL
AWS S3
AWS Route 53

Design the application so it can later support:

Redis
queues
CloudFront
WAF
load balancing
multiple API instances
database replicas

Do not introduce these prematurely.

Architecture changes

Any architectural change affecting multiple domains requires documentation before implementation.

Never silently introduce microservices.